'''Kenneth Maurice Clarke''' (born August 28, 1956) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[defensive tackle]] for 14 seasons in the [[National Football League]] (NFL).<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{Cite news |last=Mulligan |first=Kevin |date=February 3, 2005 |title=Whatever happened to...KEN CLARKE? |url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/philadelphia-daily-news-whatever-happene/175383693/ |access-date=2025-06-27 |work=Philadelphia Daily News |via=[[Newspapers.com]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite pro-football-reference|name=Ken Clarke|id=C\ClarKe24|access-date=October 15, 2025}}</ref> He played in [[Super Bowl XV]] for the [[Philadelphia Eagles]]. {{Citation needed|date=June 2025}} 

Clarke played [[college football]] for the [[Syracuse Orange football|Syracuse Orange]], also as a defensive tackle.<ref name=":0">{{Cite book |url=https://archive.org/details/eagles-1987-media-guide-philadelphia-c/page/26/mode/2up?q=%22ken+Clarke%22 |title=Eagles 1987 Media Guide |date=August 1987 |publisher=[[Philadelphia Eagles]] |pages=71 |via=[[Internet Archive]]}}</ref> He twice received an honorable mention in the AP All-America rankings and was selected to the All-East first team.<ref name=":0" />
